p:"Hip",canopyShed:"Shed (lean-to)",canopyGable:"Gable porch hood (gable facing out)",canopyGableWalls:"The veranda touches the house on several sides — a shed canopy is built instead of a gable one.",matCanopyGableStuds:"Canopy: gable and ridge posts",bdCGableStud:"Canopy: gable / ridge post",canopyPitch:"Canopy pitch, °",canopyOverhang:"Canopy overhang",canopyHint:"The canopy rests on columns (place them at the veranda corners) and 150×150 beams; at the house wall the rafters butt against the wall OSB sheathing; rafters along the wall are screwed to it; a spreader board on the wall joins the two points where the hip rafters land. Rafter section and spacing are taken from the house roof.",canopyUnderRoof:"A veranda with its own canopy is not covered by the main roof: it gets a canopy below the house roof, abutting the wall.",pie_board150:"Board 50×150",pie_board200:"Board 50×200",pie_board100:"Board 50×100",columns:"Columns",columnSection:"Column section, mm",columnCount:"Columns",layerColumns:"Columns",demoBadge:"Demo",demoNote:"Demo version: the project is stored only in your browser (no sign-up, no server).",demoReset:"Start over",demoResetAsk:"Delete the current project in this browser and start over?",priceTimber:"Timber, ₽/m³",priceInsulation:"Insulation, ₽/m³",pricePlywood:"Plywood, ₽/m²",priceGlazing:"Glazing, ₽/m²",glazingArea:"Glazing (windows)",costGlazing:"Glazing cost",priceOsb9:"OSB 9 mm (walls), ₽/m²",priceOsb:"OSB 12 mm (roof), ₽/m²",matBattens:"Battens",matValleys:"Valleys (two boards)",bdCatValleys:"Valleys (double board)",matHips:"Hip rafters (two boards)",bdCatHips:"Hip rafters (double board)",matCanopyBeams:"Canopy: beams",bdCSpreader:"Canopy: spreader board",matCanopySpreaders:"Canopy: spreader board on the wall",matCanopyRafters:"Canopy: rafters",matCanopyBattens:"Canopy: battens",bdCatCanopy:"Veranda canopies",bdCBeam:"Canopy: beam",bdCRafter:"Canopy: rafter",bdCHip:"Canopy: hip rafter",bdCRidge:"Canopy: ridge",bdCBatten:"Canopy: battens",ma